# Day 36

## Experiment Title

Managing Dependencies in Maven Projects


## Objective

To understand how dependencies are managed in Maven applications using the pom.xml file.


## Theory

Dependencies are external libraries required for application development and execution. Maven automatically downloads and manages these libraries through the pom.xml configuration file.

Developers can add dependency information inside the pom.xml file, and Maven retrieves the required files from online repositories. Dependency management simplifies application development and reduces manual library configuration.


## Requirements

Java Development Kit

Apache Maven

Windows Operating System


## Procedure

Open the Maven project directory.

Access the pom.xml configuration file.

Add dependency information for the required library.

Save the project configuration.

Run the Maven build process and observe dependency downloading.

Verify that the dependency was added successfully to the project.


## Output

Dependencies were added successfully to the Maven project.

Maven automatically downloaded the required libraries.

The application build process completed successfully after dependency integration.


## Result

Successfully understood dependency management in Maven projects using the pom.xml configuration file.
